# GI-EMISSIVE-LIGHTS (link of GI-ALL-LIGHTS): under the hardware GI tracer the surface cache's direct lighting samples the scene's emissive triangles as lights (the path tracer's one emissive list, picked by power, shadowed by the tracer's ray), and the radiosity leaves the emission of its hits out (counted once). A lamp's glowing shade now lights the wall beside it in the cache, so every GI ray meeting that wall carries the bounce.
# Headless shots (the project is outside the repo): F:/BistroFoliageProj, Editor --project F:/BistroFoliageProj/Desert.deproj --scene <scene> --camera ... --look ... --shot <png> --shot-frames 120. Baseline = the same shots from a dev build (origin/dev at this branch's merge-base).
Дано F:/BistroFoliageProj, B16_Bistro_Street_v70.desce, Lit, GlobalIllumination.Method 5 (HardwareTraced), Reflections.Method as the level; the sun up, the scene's point/spot lights on; camera on the street by the lit shop windows / lamps.
Когда run Quality "Quality: GlobalIllumination.Method HardwareTraced"; shoot after 120 frames (this branch) and the same with the dev build.
Тогда [gi_all_lights_link] 0_day_hwgi: diff vs dev > 0 in the region around the emissive fixtures (facade/pavement next to the lamp shades and windows), larger there than elsewhere; no NaN/Inf pixel (frame mean finite, no black/white speckle blocks); 0 VUID and 0 "[SceneRenderer] Surface Cache" errors in editor.log
Дано the same, GI_Bistro_Night (sun down, lamps and emissive shades only).
Когда shoot after 120 frames, this branch and dev.
Тогда 1_night_hwgi: walls and pavement beside the emissive shades brighter than dev (mean luminance in the lamp region up), no fireflies above the dev frame's max; 0 VUID
Дано the same scene, GlobalIllumination.Method 4 (SoftwareTraced).
Когда shoot after 120 frames, this branch and dev.
Тогда 2_day_swgi: byte-identical to dev up to the GI's own frame-to-frame noise (the software tracer has no emissive list: GI-EMISSIVE-LIGHTS-SW); 0 VUID
Дано F:/BistroFoliageProj, GI_Bistro_Night, GlobalIllumination.Method 4 (SoftwareTraced); machine.json (ProjectContext::ConfigDirectory) "HideRayTracing": true, editor started after the edit (the NO-RT path: no AS/ray query/RT pipeline, bufferDeviceAddress still on).
Когда state device; shoot after 120 frames (this branch) and the same without HideRayTracing; capture the CPU profile over frames 100..120.
Тогда [gi_emissive_nort] 3_night_swgi_nort: state device bufferDeviceAddress = true, rt = "hidden"; walls/pavement beside the emissive shades lit (lamp-region mean luminance within noise of the same shot with RT shown, far above a dev SW frame); no "[SceneRenderer] Surface Cache: the emissive lights" error in editor.log; profile: "RayTracingScene: SceneGather" absent on frames 100..120 (only "RayTracingScene: SceneGatherKey"); 0 VUID
Дано F:/BistroFoliageProj branch gi-emissive-incremental, scene GI_Bistro_Night_MovingEmitter (GI_Bistro_Night + entity "MovingEmitter_Streetlight_Glass_01a", Script assets:Scripts/Examples/OrbitCircle.lua: self:setPosition, EntityLibrary.hpp), GlobalIllumination.Method 4 (SoftwareTraced); machine.json "HideRayTracing": true, editor started after the edit (no TLAS on any frame: the emissive list reads the cached SCENE gather). ONE emissive prop animated: a copy of one emissive lamp shade (static mesh, its own GPU-scene row, emissive material unchanged) with a ScriptComponent (Luau OnUpdate) that moves it every frame on a 50 cm circle around its placement (translation only, sections/materials untouched); simulation running so OnUpdate ticks every frame.
Когда 300 frames render with the prop moving; state device after frame 300; CPU profile over frames 2..300.
Тогда [gi_emissive_incremental] 4_night_swgi_moving: state device.emissiveLights: gatherFullRebuilds == 1 and emissiveListFullRebuilds == 1 and gpuFullRebuilds == 1 over the 300 frames; gatherMoves, emissiveListMoves and gpuMoves each == the frames the prop moved (~299: its rows updated in place every frame); gpuMovesRetried == 0; profile: "RayTracingScene: SceneGather" and "EmissiveLights: Rebuild" only on frame 1, "RayTracingScene: SceneGatherMove" and "EmissiveLights: Move" on every frame the prop moves; the light the prop casts follows it (wall/pavement lit beside its current position, frame 300 vs frame 150 differ there and only there up to GI noise); the textured signs keep their look; 0 VUID
Дано F:/BistroFoliageProj branch gi-emissive-incremental, scene GI_Bistro_Night_MovingEmitter (case 4's moving lamp-shade copy), GlobalIllumination.Method 5 (HardwareTraced), machine.json without "HideRayTracing" (the TLAS is traced every frame), Scalability GlobalIllumination.TlasUpdatesBeforeRebuild at its default 60; simulation running so OnUpdate moves the prop every frame.
Когда 300 frames render with the prop moving; state device after frame 300; CPU profile over frames 2..300.
Тогда [gi_emissive_stream] 5_night_hwgi_moving: state device.emissiveLights.gatherFullRebuilds == 1 (the TLAS gather kept, GI-ALL-LIGHTS step 8) and emissiveListFullRebuilds == 1; state device.tlasFullBuilds == 1 + the periodic rebuilds only (<= 1 + floor(299 / 61) = 5 over 300 frames at 60 updates per build), tlasUpdates == the remaining TLAS frames, tlasMovedRows > 0 (~ one per frame the prop moves); profile: "RayTracingScene: TlasGather" and "RayTracingScene: InstanceList" only on frame 1, "RayTracingScene: TlasGatherMove" + "RayTracingScene: InstancePatch" on every later frame; the moving glass lights the street beside its current position (frame 300 vs frame 150 differ there and only there up to GI noise); 0 VUID
